  "takeaway": "A 20 percent error in the dollars-per-WAR level would change price tags, not the pecking order: among the FV 45 and up prospects that drive rankings and trade value, rank correlation with the baseline stays above 0.9999, nobody enters or leaves the top 50, and no baseline top-50 player moves more than 2 spots. Below FV 45, values sit on the fixed Edwards dollar anchor and the calibration floor, so tier medians there do not move at all, while FV 45 and up tier medians move about 7 to 38 percent under 10 to 20 percent level shifts, locally amplified or damped by the isotonic output calibration. Rankings and tier comparisons are therefore stable to how the market level is estimated, and the absolute dollar figures carry that uncertainty at roughly the size of the shift."
